WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.268
-Thank you so much
for watching, everybody.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.470
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:06.106
Guys, it is a big night for NBC.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:08.540
It is the start of BTS Week

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.410
here on "The Tonight Show"!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.679
We have something special
for you BTS fans

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:14.781
in a couple minutes.

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:17.216
Also, a huge night for hockey --

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:20.520
if you just watched Game 6
of the Stanley Cup Playoffs,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.522
that means you're either
drunk and happy

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:24.857
or drunk and very angry.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:28.561
I actually watched the game
through my plastic face shield,

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.530
so I feel like
I was really there.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.764
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:33.699
Yeah, tonight,
we got to see white guys

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:35.601
brutally attack each other
for two hours,

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:38.571
so it was a pretty good preview
of tomorrow night's debate.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.839
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.174
Let's get to some politics.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.976
Well, guys, last night,
"The New York Times"

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.477
published a bombshell report

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:47.580
about President Trump's
personal finances.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.215
Yep, somehow "The Times"
got their hands

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.017
on Trump's long-hidden
tax records,

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.118
and what they found
was not good.

00:00:53.118 --> 00:00:54.854
Listen to this.
-The "New York Times" reports

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.489
it's obtained two decades' worth

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.224
of President Trump's
tax returns.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:02.028
-"The Times" reports that the
President paid no income taxes

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:04.964
in 10 of the last 15 years.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:07.600
-That's right --
Trump has not paid income taxes

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.904
in 10 of the last 15 years,
although, honestly,

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.338
wouldn't it have been
more shocking

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.274
if Trump had paid taxes
in those years?

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:15.474
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:17.209
Yeah, when the news broke,
Trump was furious.

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:20.146
He was like, "Why did I pay
taxes for those five years?"

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.348
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.651
Seriously, when it
comes to avoiding taxes,

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.386
Trump knows every loophole.

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.287
For instance,
on next year's taxes,

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:30.423
he plans on claiming
his coronavirus response

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:31.925
as a total loss.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.659
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:35.028
[ Applause ]
What?

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:37.230
Thank you.
It's a clapper.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.766
It's a clapper.
Some laughs, some claps.

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:43.636
Well, someone close to Trump
must have provided the records.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.671
When asked who might have
a grudge against him,

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:48.974
Trump was like, "Other than
65 tell-all book authors,

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:51.511
no one comes to mind."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:56.249
So Trump didn't pay any income
taxes for 10 out of 15 years.

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.583
Big deal.

00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.218
I'm sure when Trump did pay
something, it was a lot.

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:03.055 line:0%
-In 2016, the year Trump
won the White House,

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:07.527 line:0%
he paid just $750
in income tax.

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.495
-$750!

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:10.896
I don't know what he should
have paid,

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:13.466
but it is definitely more than
an Xbox and a half.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:17.537
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.705
$750?!
That's great.

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:22.374
In today's money, Trump
basically paid the equivalent

00:02:22.374 --> 00:02:24.677
of a 1993 Toyota Tercel.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:25.978
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:28.280
Even people who use
the free version of TurboTax

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.983
are like,
"That can't be right."

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.617
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:34.387
The report also found that,
on top of not paying taxes,

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.155
Trump wrote off
a bunch of expenses

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:37.824
that seemed kind of suspicious.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.291 line:0%
-The paper also accuses

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:40.727 line:0%
the President
and his companies

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.629 line:0%
of claiming
questionable deductions

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.129 line:0%
on some of those businesses.

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:47.900 line:0%
More than $109,000
for linens and silverware

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:51.070 line:0%
and nearly $200,000
for landscaping.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:54.007 line:0%
He also wrote off more
than $70,000 in haircuts

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.543 line:0%
when he was on "The Apprentice."

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:59.879
-The crazy part isn't that
he spent $70,000 on his hair --

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.915
it's that, clearly,
$70,000 wasn't enough.

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:04.951
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.952
[ Applause ]

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:09.922
Should have went with $150,000.

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:11.724
Landscaping.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.426
The most damaging part
of the report also shows

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:14.827
that Trump might not be

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:17.730
the billionaire expert
businessman he claims to be.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.665 line:0%
-"The Times" says documents
show the President

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:24.003 line:0%
reported more than $47 million
in losses in 2018 alone,

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:28.607 line:0%
and he faces a personal debt
totaling $421 million,

00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:30.876 line:0%
money that could come due
while he is in office

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:32.978 line:0%
if he's elected
to a second term.

00:03:32.978 --> 00:03:35.648
-Wow. This news comes
as a huge shock.

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:36.849
I mean, all this time, I thought

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.818
the guy who lost money
running a casino

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.620
was a financial wiz.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.022
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.991
Yep, Trump's got to pay back
$421 million.

00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:48.494
In response, college kids
with student loans are like,

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.697
"Holy crap! I'm richer
than the president!"

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:51.930
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.533
Basically,
this is who Trump says he is,

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:56.402
and this is who he really is.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.936
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.936 --> 00:03:59.771
I guess that, when you owe
that kind of money,

00:03:59.771 --> 00:04:01.473
you start doing
desperate things.

00:04:01.473 --> 00:04:03.743
Look at what I saw today
on Zillow.

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.078
He's selling the White House.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:09.381
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.381 --> 00:04:10.984
I'll check it out
at an open house.

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:13.152
I'm not sure
if I'm going to buy it.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:17.223
Since 2000, Trump's reported
over $300 million in losses

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:19.425
just from his golf courses.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.592
Would have been
a better investment

00:04:20.592 --> 00:04:22.128
if Trump opened up a RadioShack

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:24.597
inside a Blockbuster
inside a Sears.

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:26.765
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.765 --> 00:04:28.500
It wasn't all bad news
for Trump this weekend.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.470
On Saturday, he officially
named his nominee

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.905
to replace the late
Justice Ruth Bader Ginsburg

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.407
on the Supreme Court.

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:36.108
-It is my honor to nominate

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:40.779
one of our nation's most
brilliant and gifted legal minds

00:04:40.779 --> 00:04:42.982
to the Supreme Court.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:46.586
She is a woman of
unparalleled achievement,

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:49.989
towering intellect,
sterling credentials,

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:53.826
and unyielding loyalty
to the Constitution,

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:57.463
Judge Amy Coney Barrett.

00:04:57.463 --> 00:05:00.399
-Whew!
Good Lord, that took forever.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.134
By the time Trump was done
with the introduction,

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:04.003
he had to fill
three more Supreme Court seats.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.904
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:07.640
Seriously, the only thing Trump
will drag out longer

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.541
are the results of the election.

00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:12.178
Of course, the presidential
election is heating up,

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:14.146
and the first debate
is tomorrow night.

00:05:14.146 --> 00:05:16.149
It'll be a little different than
debates we've seen in the past.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.149
Watch this.

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:18.584 line:0%
-Joe Biden and President Trump

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.887 line:0%
are preparing to face off
for the first time.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:23.523 line:0%
Now, this debate will be
very different from debates past

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:25.124 line:0%
due to the coronavirus pandemic.

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.059 line:0%
Biden and Trump
will not shake hands,

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:28.928 line:0%
there will be
a much smaller audience,

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:33.098 line:0%
and everyone on hand
will be tested for COVID-19.

00:05:33.098 --> 00:05:35.134
-Yep. The debate
is almost here right now.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:36.903
Biden plans on
throwing Trump off

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:39.672
by walking out in a hat
that says "I.R.S."

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:42.942
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.443
Because of COVID,
the candidates

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.278
won't start the night
while shaking hands --

00:05:46.278 --> 00:05:47.846
well, partly because of COVID,

00:05:47.846 --> 00:05:50.382
but mostly 'cause Trump just
doesn't know how to shake hands.

00:05:50.382 --> 00:05:55.354
♪♪

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:57.256
-Yeah, I know. Yeah.

00:05:57.256 --> 00:06:01.260 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.328 line:0%
-[ Chuckles ]
How you doing there?

00:06:03.328 --> 00:06:05.964 line:0%
Yeah, yeah.
Oh, oh, boy.

00:06:05.964 --> 00:06:08.167
[ Laughter ]
That's...

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.336
Oh, boy...

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:11.937
That's right -- the candidates
won't start the evening

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:13.138
by shaking hands.

00:06:13.138 --> 00:06:14.940
Instead, it'll be like
a wedding dance floor,

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:18.077
where Biden casts a line
at Trump and then reels him in.

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:22.548
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:24.149
With the debate
happening tomorrow night,

00:06:24.149 --> 00:06:25.918
both Trump and Biden
have been busy

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:27.487
preparing what
they're going to say.

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:29.054
And we actually managed
to get our hands

00:06:29.054 --> 00:06:31.490
on some video
of Trump's debate prep.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.225
Check this out.

00:06:33.225 --> 00:06:35.528
[ Bird chirps ]

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:38.631
-Alright, the big debate's
tomorrow, and we gotta prep.

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:39.998
We gotta prep.

00:06:39.998 --> 00:06:41.867
If I blow this,
there's no telling

00:06:41.867 --> 00:06:44.870
how many tens of people will
change their minds about me.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:46.005
That's why I asked you,

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:48.907
my loyal team of future
tell-all authors,

00:06:48.907 --> 00:06:50.175
to come up with questions.

00:06:50.175 --> 00:06:52.277
So, hit me.
What do we got?

00:06:52.277 --> 00:06:54.046
-Mr. President,
first question --

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:55.614
when will the COVID vaccine
be ready?

00:06:55.614 --> 00:06:57.650
-Easy. Tomorrow.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.185
Definitely tomorrow.
It's coming out immediately.

00:07:00.185 --> 00:07:02.388
And, look,
it's a very wonderful vaccine.

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.722
Tastes great.

00:07:03.722 --> 00:07:06.959
Very delicious vaccine --
gonna to be grape probably.

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:08.560
We have our scientists
working around the clock,

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:11.964
mixing [inhales sharply]
the vials and the beakers,

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.066
and it's turning the liquid
into different colors.

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:15.234
Just incredible.

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:16.802
Right now,
it's very green and bubbly,

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:19.404
and it unleashes smoke
in the shape of a skull,

00:07:19.404 --> 00:07:20.873
so it's looking good.

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:22.008
Next question.

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:23.341
-Mr. President, is it true that,

00:07:23.341 --> 00:07:28.113
in 2016 and '17, you paid
$750 in federal income taxes?

00:07:28.113 --> 00:07:29.948
-Absolutely false.
-Excellent.

00:07:29.948 --> 00:07:31.417
Great, clear answer.

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:32.518
-I paid $350.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:33.886
-Okay, maybe
let's just skip that.

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:35.488
-Sir, what's your view
on climate change?

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:37.757
-Look, I've said it before.
We love the climate.

00:07:37.757 --> 00:07:40.525
The scientists --
they don't even know.

00:07:40.525 --> 00:07:41.594
They don't even know.

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:44.196
I watch WKTG --
their meteorologist.

00:07:44.196 --> 00:07:46.699
He gets the climate wrong
most every day.

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:48.634
He says, "It's raining."
There's no rain.

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.670
He says, "It's sunny,"
but I look at my phone,

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:52.872
and the sun's behind
a little cloud.

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:54.006
Very sad.

00:07:54.006 --> 00:07:55.507
It's a tough thing --
the climate.

00:07:55.507 --> 00:07:57.943
[ Inhales sharply ]
Very tough. Very tough thing.

00:07:57.943 --> 00:07:59.111
-Mr. President, if you win...

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:02.080
-Ah-bah, ah-bah -- when I win.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.849
[ Laughter ]
How about when I win?

00:08:03.849 --> 00:08:05.117
-...when you win,

00:08:05.117 --> 00:08:07.086
how exactly are
you gonna unite the country?

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:09.321
-I'm going to pass on that one.
-Okay.

00:08:09.321 --> 00:08:11.556
How will you ease
racial tension?

00:08:11.556 --> 00:08:13.226
-Ooh, big pass.

00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:15.895
-Back to your taxes --
-Double-dog pass.

00:08:15.895 --> 00:08:17.629
-Well, I think we need
an answer for that.

00:08:17.629 --> 00:08:21.300
-I said double-dog,
so, legally, you have to pass.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.567
They said I can have
three passes.

00:08:22.567 --> 00:08:23.636
Didn't they say that?

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:26.004
Can we look into that?
Three passes?

00:08:26.004 --> 00:08:27.673
-What do you think
of Biden's plan to --

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:29.709
-Look, the thing about --
the thing about Biden,

00:08:29.709 --> 00:08:32.778
can I just say
the thing about Biden

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:35.481
is that he's a nasty woman.

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:37.183
[ Laughter ]
He's such a nasty woman.

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:39.284
-Sorry, you said
that about Hillary.

00:08:39.284 --> 00:08:40.419
-That's right.

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:42.354
I'm bringing back
all the classics.

00:08:42.354 --> 00:08:44.156
No one goes
to a Counting Crows concert

00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:45.825
to hear the new stuff, folks.

00:08:45.825 --> 00:08:49.495
With me, it's "Mr. Jones"
all night.

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:52.431
By the way, that's where I --
that's where I drop the mic.

00:08:52.431 --> 00:08:54.066
-You won't have a mic, sir.

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:56.434
-Well, I'll --
I'll drop this one, then.

00:08:56.434 --> 00:08:58.738
[ Clicking, fabric rustling ]
-Not that kind of mic.

00:08:58.738 --> 00:09:00.639
[ No audio ]

00:09:00.639 --> 00:09:03.776
We can't hear you now, sir.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:06.111
[ Clicking, fabric rustling ]

00:09:06.111 --> 00:09:07.379
-Hello?

00:09:07.379 --> 00:09:10.282
-Sir, civil unrest is widespread
across the country.

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:12.751
-Yes, it's very unrestful.
People are very upset.

00:09:12.751 --> 00:09:15.420
They're throwing cans of tuna.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:17.456
Very sad for tuna.
Next?

00:09:17.456 --> 00:09:20.025
-Finally, will you accept
the outcome of the election

00:09:20.025 --> 00:09:21.393
if you don't win?

00:09:21.393 --> 00:09:24.396
-I will absolutely.
Definitely.

00:09:24.396 --> 00:09:25.898
[ Clicking, fabric rustling ]

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:27.199
[ No audio ]

00:09:27.199 --> 00:09:29.368
-Sir, we can't hear --
[ Laughter ]

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:30.936
Oh, he knows.

00:09:30.936 --> 00:09:32.171
[ No audio ]

00:09:32.171 --> 00:09:34.340
[ Applause ]

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.875
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:39.845
-How did we get our hands
on that debate prep?

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:41.981
And, finally,
right before the debate,

00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:44.883
Joe Biden just picked up a big
endorsement from Dwayne Johnson.

00:09:44.883 --> 00:09:46.185 line:0%
Check it out.

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:48.554 line:0%
-I do feel that
Vice President Biden

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:50.122 line:0%
and Senator Harris

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:52.424 line:0%
are the best choice
to lead our country,

00:09:52.424 --> 00:09:53.659 line:0%
and I am endorsing them

00:09:53.659 --> 00:09:55.961 line:0%
to become President
and Vice President

00:09:55.961 --> 00:09:58.430 line:0%
of our United States.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.700
-Yeah. Biden said,
"Thanks for endorsing me."

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.769
Then Dwayne said,
"Just return the favor in 2024."

00:10:03.769 --> 00:10:06.171
[ Laughter ]

00:10:06.171 --> 00:10:07.372
